WEBVTT

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:36.020
Tama-chan!  Good afternoon, Tama-chan!

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.870
We mages have an important partner, our magic wands.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:51.830
They each have their own shapes and personalities.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.210
But even among them,

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:01.860
the one owned by Takamine-senpai, who runs the Fortunetelling Research Club, is very unique.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.120
Tama-chan!

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:05.040
Good morning!

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.500
<i>Good morning, everyone!</i>

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.940
Good morning, Koyuki-san!

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:16.680
Hey, this is some relative of yours isn't it?

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:16.670
FLYER:  Magical Art Exhibition Recreating the Legendary Ancient Supheiatam

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.580
I'm telling you it's your imagination.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:19.980
The name is totally different.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:22.610
<i>This is my ancestor!</i>

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.360
Tama-chan's formal name is Supheiatam.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.790
He is a member of a very old and prestigious family, even for a magic wand.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:33.750
I knew it!

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.700
<i>Yes, I'm very prestigious!</i>

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:41.110
Well then, my class is this way.

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:42.730
<i>Peace out!</i>

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:46.650
That's the head of the Fortunetelling Research Club for you.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:51.560
If she's got something that prestigious, then I'm sure the rest of the club members...

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.020
Actually, I think...

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.380
She's the only member of the club.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:02:58.970
Really?

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:10.840
<b>Missing Tama-chan</b>

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.770
You're going to join...

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:17.270
The Fortunetelling Research Club...

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.190
Sumomo-chan?

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:21.720
Yes, let's all join!

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.160
Us, too?

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:26.000
It'll be more fun with more people!

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.950
That's true, but...

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.470
Come on, let's join!

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:34.310
Even if you're just going to give it a try!  OK?  OK?

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:38.230
She gets that pushiness from her mom...

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:42.960
Then let's all go to the Fortunetelling Research Club's room right now!

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.200
OK...

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.090
SIGN:  Welcome!  New Members

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:49.670
<i>New members, welcome!</i>

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:53.740
How, Takamine-senpai?

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:57.680
I just kind of felt it.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.540
Come in.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:14.440
Uhm, is it true that there are no other members besides you?

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:17.370
No, there are others.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.880
Is that so?

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.650
They're all ghost members though.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.360
I suppose I should introduce them.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:36.530
From the left, Hanako-san, Uritarou-kun, Gonzaemon-san...

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.230
Sumomo!

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.640
They're real ghosts!

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.020
BOARD:  Let's make a Tama-chan!

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:51.050
Our activity plan today is to create a Tama-chan.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:55.800
I'm going to have all of you new members help me make Tama-chans.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.140
You can make a Tama-chan?

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.140
Yes, you make each one by hand.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:12.140
They're waiting for their turn here.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:18.810
You prepare the secret ingredients, and then let them ferment for a week to make the Tama-chan base.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:23.780
Separate them into just the right size and knead them, and the Tama-chan is done.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:29.580
Depending on how you knead it, you may end up with a good Tama-chan or a bad Tama-chan.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.680
So put your heart into it and knead carefully.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.870
Put your heart into it...

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.110
And knead it carefully.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.140
<i>OK, get goin' guys!</i>

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:47.320
Oh, kneading up a Tama-chan!

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.070
All right!

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:53.070
Oh, kneading up a Tama-chan!

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:55.410
<i>Aye, aye, sir!</i>

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.560
Aye, aye, sir!

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:02.020
Oh, we're kneading up a Tama-chan today!

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:03.960
<i>Aye, aye, sir!</i>

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.900
I guess it's time.  All right...

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.850
I'm going to put a soul into the Tama-chans.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:19.590
<i>El Amlaibu Misa Enril Sfen Carna De Libris!</i>

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.460
<i>Yo, howzit goin', dude?</i>

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:32.390
Wow, the Tama-chan I made talked!

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.490
<i>Nice to meet you.</i>

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:37.170
This is really cool!

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:39.330
<i>I am honored that you kneaded me.</i>

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:40.350
Th-Thank you.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:45.280
<i>I still feel kinda stiff.  I think you messed up your kneading, lady.</i>

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:49.910
I think this one's kind of nasty.

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:52.110
<i>And you call yourself a mage?</i>

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:56.250
You want a piece of me?  You're just a wanna-be magic wand!

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:57.300
<i>Wanna-be?</i>

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.450
<i>Well, if that's how you want it, then that's fine.</i>

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:01.560
Oh no!

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.120
What the heck?

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:05.610
Tama-chan, go!

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.030
<i>Roger, miss!</i>

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:20.750
That was close.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.640
Are you all right, Anri-chan?

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:28.570
When a Tama-chan flashes red, that's a warning that it's about to self-destruct.

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:32.490
We were seconds away from the room being destroyed.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:35.170
Are Tama-chans actually dangerous?

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:36.390
No.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:42.100
I've made lots of Tama-chans,
but that's never happened before.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.690
Lots?

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.210
How many?

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:49.050
This will be the 1000th I've made.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:50.080
The 1000th?

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:50.940
That many?

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.200
Wow, that's quite a commemorative occasion!

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.000
Hey, let's have a party!

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.560
A party to celebrate the completion of your 1000th Tama-chan!

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:58.970
I agree!

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:14.280
I see.  Takamine-senpai makes her Tama-chan like that.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:17.750
Putting her heart and soul into every one...

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:22.220
It seems really hard, but she's been doing it for years.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:30.940
Your magic wand will be a very important partner for you as you grow as a mage.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:35.050
Put your heart into it as you cast the spell.

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:38.900
That's why I've had you bring something that's important to you.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:43.850
I hope you all meet wonderful partners.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:54.150
<i>El Amdaltry Wants Ri Eltea Kheimos...</i>

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.220
<i>Hello, Haruhi.</i>

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.020
I wonder if I put my heart into it right.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:18.250
<i>Don't worry, Haruhi.</i>

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.970
<i>I felt your heart when you cast the spell.</i>

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:23.120
Thank you, Soprano.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:31.080
A magic wand, huh?

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.340
<i>Nice to meet you, Anri-sama.</i>

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:46.540
Why does he sound so old?

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:51.440
To be honest, at first I thought I had failed.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.770
But now I'm glad I got you.

00:09:53.770 --> 00:09:57.780
<i>Thank you, Anri-sama.</i>

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.350
And if I ever need to, I can eat you.

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:03.090
<i>Anri-sama, please don't eat so much of me...</i>

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:05.520
Shut up!  It grows back, right?

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.630
<i>Ah, yes.</i>

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:19.790
<i>Was everyone happy like that when I was born?</i>

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:22.800
<i>The 1000th one, huh?</i>

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:27.110
You're just a wanna-be magic wand!

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:39.470
<i>I'm sure she doesn't remember what number I am.</i>

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:01.230
<i>Miss, just for a while, let me be on my own.</i>

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:32.060
Tama-chan?

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.330
Uhm...

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:47.810
Takamine-senpai?

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.810
Have you seen Tama-chan?

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:52.280
No, we haven't.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:54.750
Koyuki-san, did something happen to him?

00:11:57.140 --> 00:11:59.890
I haven't seen him all morning.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:03.180
The one that saved us last night?

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:05.430
He didn't run away did he?

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:07.350
No way!  Why?

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:10.510
Was he unhappy about something, I wonder?

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:11.770
Unhappy, huh?

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:14.700
I guess if they're treated horribly like that...

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:19.770
But you've got lots of other ones to take its place.

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:25.720
But if I do that then he'll have nowhere to come back to.

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:28.110
Takamine-senpai...

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.980
We'll help you look for him.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.070
Yeah, let's all look for him!

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:37.120
He saved us yesterday.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:39.640
Leave it to me, Takamizo Hachisuke!

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:41.580
Let us help you!

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:44.510
Everyone...

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:53.370
POSTER:  Magical Art Exhibition Recreating the Legendary Ancient Supheiatam

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:58.790
<i>What?  I guess my ancestor isn't scheduled to appear until much later...</i>

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:11.980
OK!

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.370
I'll look around the station.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.190
Me, too.

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:20.540
Me, too then!

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:23.260
Right, right, you come this way.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:31.100
These are my dowsing rods, Suke-san and Kaku-san.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:32.710
They're going to find Tama-chan for us.

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:44.980
Shall we go now?

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.810
Tama-chan!

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:49.890
Hey, Tama-chan!

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.530
Maybe...

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:57.410
The magic crafts show?

00:13:57.410 --> 00:14:02.450
He looked really happy yesterday when Sumomo showed him the advertisement for it yesterday.

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:04.730
So maybe...

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:07.180
He may be there!

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:13.490
I guess the old guy is out of energy...

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:16.050
The other one looks like its at its limit, too.

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:19.120
This is far as the dowsing rods can take us.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.960
But we've probably gotten pretty close to him.

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:32.030
Tama-chan...

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:43.250
There he is!

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:50.760
<i>Wh-What?  What?</i>

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:56.890
<i>Hey, you two, do you two know what number I am?</i>

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:00.870
Well...

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.660
I guess we don't know that.

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:04.980
<i>I'm number 984.</i>

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:07.490
<i>But nobody knows that.</i>

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:09.050
<i>Probably not even the miss...</i>

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:12.510
<i>As soon as we hear the word "go," that's it.</i>

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:15.830
<i>We're soon forgotten.  One of many, many others.</i>

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:19.590
<i>I was thinking about that, and it all just seemed so sad and pointless...</i>

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:22.650
And so you ran away?

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:29.390
<i>I thought if I came here, my ancestors who've been around for generations could tell me something.</i>

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:31.340
Tama-chan...

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:39.570
The ancient Supheiatam will be recreated on stage shortly.

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:44.380
Everyone, please gather at...

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:43.540
Let's go, Tama-chan.

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:55.210
The recreation of the ancient Supheiatam is a very rare skill passed down only among certain mages.

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:57.840
I think it's almost fi-

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:02.100
It's almost...

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.800
It's almost finished.

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:15.010
<i>El Amraib Sadoh Embril, um, Sphecius...</i>

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:18.670
Something's wrong.

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:23.750
What's wrong, sir?

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:27.720
No, according to the book, this is right...

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.710
<i>A-Ancestor!</i>

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:45.790
That's the ancient Supheiatam?

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.090
That doesn't seem right.

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:50.490
<i>It wasn't kneaded right!</i>

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:54.230
Come to think of it, Takamine-senpai said,

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:58.920
that depending on how you kneaded it, it could turn into a good Tama-chan or a bad Tama-chan.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:08.770
Sir, we need to get away!

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:11.430
<i>Ancestor, please stop!</i>

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:13.750
<i>Listen to me!</i>

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.580
It's no good. Once it gets to that point...

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:21.500
This is what happens when you try to attract customers with magic!

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:32.010
Wh-What the heck is that?

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:38.840
<i>Ancestor, please stop!</i>

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:43.210
Tama-chan!

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:45.490
<i>I'm not powerful enough!</i>

00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:46.900
<i>Miss!</i>

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:50.250
Something's going on over there.

00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:52.610
Tama-chan...

00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:56.610
Koyuki-san?

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:07.130
What's that?

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:10.590
Somebody failed to make a Tama-chan!

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:18.020
<i>Stop, ancestor!</i>

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:20.460
<i>A Supheiatam shouldn't behave like this!</i>

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:22.580
Tama-chan?

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:27.280
<i>Miss...</i>

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:32.040
Wait, Tama-chan!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.150
<i>Leave me alone!</i>

00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:38.220
<i>I'm just one of many.  You don't even know what number I am.</i>

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:41.740
I do.  You're 984, right?

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:44.100
<i>What did you just say, miss?</i>

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:54.030
You're Tama-chan 984.  I can tell at a glance.  And I remember everybody, not just you.

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:59.910
Tama-chan 21 wants to make something of himself.

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:04.170
Tama-chan 68 is a bit selfish.

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:07.620
There's 189 who pretends to be tough, even when he really isn't.

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:13.530
And 277 is very friendly and chipper, but he's actually a bit lonely.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:15.950
<i>No way!</i>

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:20.820
<i>You made a thousand, and you remember them all?</i>

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:27.750
Of course.  I put my heart and soul into making you all, one by one...

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:30.660
<i>Miss...</i>

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:34.380
<i>That's right.  I always knew that.</i>

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:37.600
<i>So what was I so worried about?</i>

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:43.430
Hey, look at that!

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:45.250
I-It's going to blow!

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:48.050
Takamine-senpai, look at that!

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:50.590
<i>Miss, quick, use me!</i>

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:51.690
Tama-chan...

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:55.140
<i>There's no time to waste!</i>

00:19:55.140 --> 00:20:00.320
<i>The 984th Supheiatam will protect you all, no matter what!</i>

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:02.220
Tama-chan...

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:08.250
Then let's go, Tama-chan.

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:10.110
Right, miss!

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.510
Tama-chan, go!

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:15.510
<i>Aye-aye, sir!</i>

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:30.960
T-Tama-chan?

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:46.960
Goodbye, my 984th Tama-chan.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:48.960
Takamine-senpai...

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:54.200
You're all quitting the Fortunetelling Research Club?

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:56.130
Why?

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:58.560
Why, you ask?

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:04.820
Detailed emails on your cell phone every morning describing terrible things that are going to befall you each day...

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:08.310
Being setup as targets for Tama-chan's shooting practice...

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:10.390
It's too much for us.

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:12.370
Please understand, Sumomo-chan!

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:17.690
But if you all quit, then the Fortune Telling Research Club will close down!

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:20.490
The Fortune Telling Research Club will close down?

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:22.120
Did you not know, Sumomo-chan?

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:23.550
Know what?

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:29.410
Takamine-senpai is the daughter of the school's director, Takamine Yuzuha.

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:34.640
The Fortunetelling Research Club was created at her request when she joined the school.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:39.180
So, even if she's the only member, the club is fine.

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:42.450
I didn't know that.

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:48.370
But even if the club's fine, isn't she going to be lonely by herself?

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:52.820
I've got a good idea!

00:21:56.340 --> 00:21:57.910
I can see it...

00:21:57.910 --> 00:22:01.680
Your lucky item is a steamed bun.

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:03.640
Thank you!

00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:05.480
I see.

00:22:05.480 --> 00:22:09.570
If she does fortune-telling in Oasis, then she won't be in her room alone all the time.

00:22:10.250 --> 00:22:12.570
Smart, Hime-chan!

00:22:12.570 --> 00:22:14.530
Not at all...

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:21.820
Takamine Koyuki-senpai's fortunetelling corner is really popular at Mizuhosaka Academy!

00:23:55.010 --> 00:24:24.970
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:59.780
Today I'm going to do the preview with no introductions.

00:23:59.780 --> 00:24:01.470
I'm Kamisaka Haruhi.

00:24:01.890 --> 00:24:06.010
The next episode is that staple of school anime, the "kaidan" (ghost story) episode.

00:24:06.010 --> 00:24:08.790
K-Kaidan?  That means...

00:24:06.010 --> 00:24:16.430
NOTE:  She's confusing the multiple meanings of the word <i>kaidan</i>  (ghost story, conference, stairway).

00:24:08.790 --> 00:24:12.460
We meet some important people and have a
conference.  It's not that "kaidan" (conference) is it?

00:24:12.460 --> 00:24:16.430
Is it the "kaidan" (stairs) you go up step by step?  That's not it, of course.

00:24:16.440 --> 00:24:20.820
I know, I know, but I'm not good with scary stories.

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:24.970
<b>The Midnight Beauty</b>

00:24:20.820 --> 00:24:22.350
The Midnight Beauty!

00:24:22.350 --> 00:24:24.970
It's probably a scary story!
